# Performance Optimisation

## Core Web Vitals Budgets (enforced by Lighthouse CI)
| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| LCP | < 2.5s |
| FID | < 100ms |
| CLS | < 0.1 |
| Initial bundle (gzipped) | < 200KB |
| React Query cache hit rate | > 60% |

## Code Splitting — Required for All Feature Pages
```tsx
// pages/leads/index.ts — always lazy
const LeadsPage = lazy(() => import('@/pages/leads/LeadsPage'))
// Wrap with skeleton fallback, never a generic spinner
<Suspense fallback={<PageSkeleton />}><LeadsPage /></Suspense>
```

## Vite Manual Chunks (keep in sync with vite.config.ts)
```ts
manualChunks: {
  vendor:  ['react', 'react-dom'],
  query:   ['@tanstack/react-query'],
  charts:  ['recharts', '@tremor/react'],
  crypto:  ['crypto-js'],
}
```

## Memoisation Rules
- `React.memo` — wrap pure presentational components that receive stable props
- `useCallback` — stabilise callbacks passed to child components or `useEffect` deps
- `useMemo` — only for genuinely expensive computation; add a comment explaining why
- Measure before optimising — don't add `memo` everywhere speculatively

## Virtual Lists
- Use `@tanstack/virtual` for any list or table rendering > 100 items
- Never render all rows in a DataTable — always paginate or virtualise

## Search/Filter Inputs
- Debounce all search/filter inputs by **300ms** before triggering API calls
- Use `useDeferredValue` for local filter operations on large datasets

## Images
- Always set `loading="lazy"` and explicit `width` + `height` to prevent CLS
- Prefer WebP; use `srcset` for responsive images

## Skeleton Screens
- Use skeleton screens that **match the exact layout** of the loaded content
- Never use a generic full-page spinner — it causes layout shift on resolution

## Pagination
- Default page size: **25 rows**
- Offer selector: 10 / 25 / 50 / 100
- Use cursor-based pagination where the API supports it (better for large datasets)
